SMOKE_CURSOR_LEGACY

This is the legacy Cursor rules file (.cursorrules). It is always read by Cursor.
New projects should use .cursor/rules/*.mdc instead.

## Project conventions (legacy)

- Python 3.11+. Use `python3` explicitly in shell scripts.
- All configuration comes from environment variables. Never hardcode paths, credentials,
  or hostnames.
- Log to stdout using the standard `logging` module. Do not write log files.
- CSV input files live in $DATA_DIR/input/. Processed output goes to $DATA_DIR/output/.
- When something fails, exit non-zero with a clear error message. Do not swallow errors.
